  "confirmed": [
    "Re-rendering frames 0/1 from initial_state gives a dataset whose only difference is those two frames per episode: audit selection, converted episode/frame counts, info.json and split indices are identical to the original 76-candidate pipeline.",
    "Offline hold-out first-frame RMSE drops from 0.1452 to 0.1063 rad (uniform-frame RMSE unchanged, 0.0500 -> 0.0497).",
    "Rollout success stays 0/3 on seeds 4100-4102 for the fixed-frame model; the control also stays 0/3.",
    "On the identical demo_9 scene the fixed-frame model tracks the demo far better over the first 240 steps (command RMSE 0.118 vs 0.498 for the legacy model at window 240) but never commands the gripper below 0.75 rad and never touches the cube; the legacy model closed early (step 138) and pushed the cube."
  ],
  "inferred_not_proven": [
    "That the remaining failure is a grasp-decision problem (gripper close timing) rather than reach accuracy; one demo scene and three seeds only.",
    "That the 30 Hz camera duplication or the small train set (61 episodes from 10 source demos) is the dominant remaining cause."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One model per condition, three evaluation seeds, one same-scene comparison; not a success-rate estimate.",
    "Frames 0/1 come from a different render process than frames 2+ (front-camera floor ~3 MAE).",
    "No physical robot."
  ],
